{
  "_note": "background-service-account (dossiq fix after #3334). A cron job has no Nextcloud session, so OpenRegister sees Anonymous and refuses the write: the termijn reminder sweep (PauseChaseJob) sent its letter and then failed to store chasesSent, so the next run chased again. The sweep now writes as one Nextcloud account an admin picks (BackgroundServiceAccount, app config background_service_account), with OpenRegister's checks on, never with _rbac false. These are the schemas the sweep writes: deadlineInstance (chasesSent, lastChasedAt, chaseEscalatedAt) and termijnGebeurtenis (the chased and chase-escalated events). Each grants dossiq-background-service create and update. The block keeps what the open default allowed before: every logged-in user may create, read, update and delete, and an anonymous caller may read (public), so nothing changes for a handler or a portal read; it only names what the background account may do, which also holds once an operator turns on OpenRegister's enforce_default_closed. Admins keep OpenRegister's admin bypass. The case projection (pauseWaitingOn, chasesSent on the case) is deliberately not granted here: the case schema is default-open and central, so the account writes it as any logged-in user does. The repair step CreateBackgroundServiceGroup creates the group. Since the jobs sweep (fx34) every background job that writes runs as the same account, so the fragment also names the schemas those jobs and the termijn timer listener write: adviesAanvraag (AdviceDeadlineJob), bezwaarTrigger, beschikking and stateMachineLog (BezwaarTermijnJob), mailIntakeEntry and caseDocument (InboundEmailJob, TriageWakeJob), tenantQuota (ResetMonthlyQuotasJob), klantSentiment (SentimentAnalysisJob), specialistBeschikbaarheid (SpecialistBeschikbaarheidRefreshJob), stufMessage (StufRetryJob), penaltyPaymentCalculation and aanvullingsverzoek (TermijnTimerFiredListener), caseBerichtenboxMessage (BerichtenboxService, when integriq reports a letter's status or a letter is sent with nobody signed in), and workDigest (DailyDigestJob writes the digest row as the account; it composes each digest as its recipient, so the account never decides what a person is shown). None of them had an authorization block. Each keeps what a logged-in user could do and grants the group create and update. Read is authenticated only, not public: on an open-default schema an anonymous search already returns nothing, so naming public would open these rows to anonymous callers for the first time. The case schema stays out for the reason above. Closed by case-access-by-handling-team (Ruben, 2026-10-11, REQ-ACC-11): every `authenticated` and `public` here became `dossiq-medewerkers`. Keeping what the open default allowed was the right move while the register was open; with the register closed it would have left these schemas as the one part of dossiq any signed in account, and for deadlineInstance and termijnGebeurtenis any anonymous caller, could still read. No portal path reads them anonymously; portaliq reads dossiq through its own scoped reader. Read now names the background service group as well: on the open default the account read these rows as any signed in user, and a block of its own replaces the register block that would otherwise have granted it.",
